{
  "dom_id": "step-74976",
  "name": "Example: \n                    Adding a Positive Number to a Negative Number",
  "problem": "What is the value of $-6 + 9?$",
  "worked_solution": "**Method 1 - Picturing a Number Line**\n\nTo add $9$ to $-6,$ we start at $-6$ on a number line and move $9$ spaces to the right.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14149949/assets/f3fc6c865056b9a177ab65d7a4477102c3e0d28035a14230bdf8c630c262e270.png)\n\nWe end up at $3.$ So, $-6+9=3.$\n\n**Method 2 - Subtraction in Reverse**\n\nWe can swap the order of the numbers and then compute the resulting subtraction:\n\n$$\n-6+9 = 9-6 = 3\n$$",
